          "right": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "The flagship"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "VibroDrill is built for stability, performance and long service life. It is equipped with a built-in damping mechanism (rubber) that prevents vibrations from being transferred to the mast. This means less strain on the equipment, smoother drilling and better control in production."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "With a drilling angle of 0° to 90°, VibroDrill VD100 can be used both vertically and horizontally, perfect for everything from classic foundation work to more advanced installations where access and geometry require flexibility. The operator can also adjust the eccentric moment to optimise performance depending on ground conditions."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "Frequency options"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "VibroDrill is delivered as standard with 100 Hz, but can also be adapted to 85 Hz or 120 Hz depending on application and desired drilling behaviour."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "References"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "After a very successful trial in Copenhagen in the Nordhavn tunnel, carried out by Grundbau Nord GmbH, this powerful technology is now available on the market."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "Take a look at the brochure below or <a href=\"/contacto\">contact us</a> for more information."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "columns",
          "ratio": "60-40",
          "left": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "html": "The VibroDrill series"
            },
            {
