        {
          "type": "video",
          "provider": "youtube",
          "id": "511DKtXlnUs",
          "title": "VibroDrill VD | Clay liquification #vibrodrill #terra-infrastructure"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "The “liquid clay” effect"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "When the vibro is on, the clay is converted into a liquid mass resembling porridge. By breaking the structure of the clay, the skin friction around the drill or pile is almost completely eliminated, causing it to sink into the ground with minimal resistance. This technique maximises penetration speed and enables extremely efficient installation of sheet piles and piles in cohesive soils."
        }
